{"time":"2026-06-18 23:43:29,778","level":"DEBUG","logger":"aiosqlite","message":"operation functools.partial(<built-in method execute of sqlite3.Connection object at 0x70ef7fb29120>, 'INSERT OR REPLACE INTO checkpoints (thread_id, checkpoint_ns, checkpoint_id, parent_checkpoint_id, type, checkpoint, metadata) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)', ('d8402b07-b5cd-43c2-842a-e9819caeafa4', '', '1f16b6f8-25b1-683e-8040-8f954a8c15be', '1f16b6d9-945f-6353-803f-d7670e3a0bc9', 'msgpack', b'\x87\xa1v\x04\xa2ts\xd9 2026-06-18T23:43:29.774554+00:00\xa2id\xd9$1f16b6f8-25b1-683e-8040-8f954a8c15be\xaechannel_values\xde\x00\x15\xa9tenant_id\xaatenant-123\xaasession_id\xd9$d8402b07-b5cd-43c2-842a-e9819caeafa4\xaauser_query\xd9NRUn a cloud monitoring check and let me know thwe used services in last 4 days\xadrouter_theory\xd9\xf3The user wants to know which GCP services were actively used in the last 4 days. Since billing commands are restricted, we can use Cloud Audit Logs via `gcloud logging read` to extract the `serviceName` from activity logs over the last 4 days.\xadintent_status\xacCONTINUATION\xb3clarifying_question\xa0\xb2router_instruction\xda\x01\x1dRun `gcloud logging read \'logName="projects/isolated-lab-for-testing/logs/cloudaudit.googleapis.com%2Factivity"\' --freshness=4d --format="value(protoPayload.serviceName)" --limit=10000 | sort | uniq` to get a list of unique GCP services that have been actively used in the last 4 days.\xabdelegate_to\xafsecurity_review\xb4conversation_history\xda\x01\x9b[ROUTER]: [USER QUERY]: RUn a cloud monitoring check and let me know thwe used services in last 4 days\n[ROUTER]: [USER QUERY]: RUn a cloud monitoring check and let me know thwe used services in last 4 days\n[ROUTER]: [USER QUERY]: RUn a cloud monitoring check and let me know thwe used services in last 4 days\n[ROUTER]: [USER QUERY]: RUn a cloud monitoring check and let me know thwe used services in last 4 days\xaecloud_analysis\xda\x02\xdb\n\nI attempted to list the BigQuery datasets to check for billing export data, but the `bq ls` command is restricted by the environment\'s security allowlist.\n\n**Command Attempted:**\n`bq ls --project_id=isolated-lab-for-testing`\n\n**Result:**\n```\nVALIDATION FAILED: Command does not match any allowlisted prefix for cloud domain (Tiers 1-3)\n\xe2\x9a\xa0\xef\xb8\x8f Command was rejected by validation\n```\n\n**Summary:**\nI am unable to query BigQuery datasets or use `gcloud billing` commands to retrieve the exact cost incurred over the last 3 days due to command restrictions in this environment. To get the exact cost, you will need to check the GCP Billing Dashboard manually or use an account with the necessary permissions and allowlisted commands.\xaffinops_analysis\xda\r\x0b\n\n## Cost Anomaly Detection\nI am unable to retrieve the exact monetary cost incurred over the last 3 days because the `gcloud billing` commands are restricted by the environment\'s security allowlist. However, I have detected a significant process anomaly: **4 VMs are running continuously (24/7)**, which directly violates the Lab environment\'s "Nightly Shutdowns" policy outlined in Chapter 7. \n\n## Top Consumers & Workload Effectiveness\nBased on the active compute footprint, the top cost drivers for the last 3 days are:\n1. **`voice-engine-vm`** (`e2-custom-2-6400`) - Running in `me-central2-a`. Custom machine types carry a premium.\n2. **`my-windows-vm`** (`e2-medium`) - Running in `us-central1-a`. This is highly likely incurring a Windows Server licensing premium on top of the compute cost.\n3. **`instance-20260426-224222`** (`e2-medium`) - Running in `us-central1-a`.\n4. **`rof-agent-lab-vm`** (`e2-medium`) - Running in `me-central2-a`.\n\n## Waste Identification\n1. **CRITICAL COMPLIANCE VIOLATION:** Absolutely zero VMs (neither running nor terminated) possess the mandatory FinOps labels (`owner_email`, `project_end_date`, `cost_center`). This is a direct violation of Chapter 6.1 of the ADR guidelines.\n2. **Orphaned Storage Waste:** There are 4 `TERMINATED` VMs (`disk-autosc`, `testing`, `agent-test`, `wins-2`). While compute costs are halted, their underlying Persistent Disks are still accumulating daily storage charges.\n3. **Idle Compute:** The running VMs appear to be left on indefinitely without auto-cleanup or nightly shutdown mechanisms.\n\n## Architectural Optimization Push\nSupervisor, please dispatch the Cloud/OS Engineers to execute the following:\n1. **Immediate Labeling:** Apply `owner_email`, `project_end_date`, and `cost_center` to all resources. Unlabeled resources in a Lab environment should be considered rogue and flagged for deletion.\n2. **Enforce Nightly Shutdowns:** Implement instance schedules to stop `my-windows-vm`, `voice-engine-vm`, and the other running VMs outside of business hours.\n3. **Disk Cleanup:** Review and delete the Persistent Disks attached to the 4 terminated VMs if the data is no longer required.\n\n## Budget Recalibration\nBecause API-level billing access is blocked, I cannot map the exact 3-day spend against the Level 1 ($50), Level 2 ($100), and Level 3 ($250) budget alert thresholds. The user must check the GCP Billing Dashboard manually or provide access to the BigQuery billing export dataset to recalibrate the budget accurately.\n\n## Live Evidence\n```json\n[\n  {\n    "name": "instance-20260426-224222",\n    "machineType": "e2-medium",\n    "status": "RUNNING",\n    "labels": null\n  },\n  {\n    "name": "my-windows-vm",\n    "machineType": "e2-medium",\n    "status": "RUNNING",\n    "labels": null\n  },\n  {\n    "name": "rof-agent-lab-vm",\n    "machineType": "e2-medium",\n    "status": "RUNNING",\n    "labels": null\n  },\n  {\n    "name": "voice-engine-vm",\n    "machineType": "e2-custom-2-6400",\n    "status": "RUNNING",\n    "labels": null\n  },\n  {\n    "name": "disk-autosc",\n    "status": "TERMINATED",\n    "labels": null\n  },\n  {\n    "name": "testing",\n    "status": "TERMINATED",\n    "labels": null\n  },\n  {\n    "n